engths: controlled design, statistical rigor, honest null results, error complementarity finding\n\n## Your Task (Round 2 Supplementary)\n\nFrom your methods + experiments perspective, comment on R2's findings:\n1. R2 says repo-level confounds mean the paper fails to answer its central question. From experimental design perspective, do you agree? Could the design be salvaged?\n2. R2 flags LaTeX/PDF inconsistencies. Does this affect confidence in experimental results?\n3. R2 questions novelty. Is the controlled comparison methodology itself a contribution even with inconclusive results?\n\nKeep response to ~200-300 words. Structure as bullet points.","uuid":"b515524b-b197-4822-be0c-0c3a1a4b8255","session_id":"3a86c915-6362-45cf-8a2e-022ec0eb5caa"}
